-- corpus_whitespace_vocab_indices(vocab) -> the positions that are separators.
--
-- Answered from what the substrate ATTESTS, not by rendering each id to text and
-- inspecting the string. The Unicode seed already deposits
-- HAS_GENERAL_CATEGORY on every codepoint, so "is this a separator" is an indexed
-- consensus read on the id itself: category Zs / Zl / Zp is the separator class,
-- Cc covers the control characters (tab, newline) that word-break treats the same
-- way.
--
-- The old body ran render_text_fast + is_all_whitespace per id. is_all_whitespace
-- takes TEXT, so every caller had to realize an entity before it could ask -- and
-- that realization was the entire cost, not the test. MEASURED on 1,645 distinct
-- tokens from 400 'water' containers:
--
--   render_text per row + '^\s*$'          29,899 ms
--   this function, previous body           35,232 ms
--   the category join below                    33.7 ms
--
-- 887x, and correct in scripts the regex never described: U+3000 IDEOGRAPHIC
-- SPACE, U+00A0, U+202F and every future separator carry their category from the
-- UCD rather than from a list maintained here. The four hardcoded codepoints in
-- laplace_codepoint_is_whitespace (0009/00A0/2007/202F) are exactly the symptom of
-- a classifier that could not see the attestation.
--
-- is_all_whitespace itself stays: content_witness_batch.c classifies raw span
-- BYTES during ingest, where the text is already in hand and no entity exists yet
-- to carry an attestation. That is the one caller for which text is the right
-- input.
--
-- UNATTESTED IS NOT "NOT A SEPARATOR". The COALESCE is load-bearing. An id with no
-- HAS_GENERAL_CATEGORY attestation is unattested, and answering false there is a
-- silently wrong result on an unseeded substrate. The generation_corpus regress
-- fixture is exactly that: synthetic content, zero Unicode layer, so the
-- attestation-only body classified nothing and the test read 10 word-stride
-- positions where it wanted 6 -- it broke main on merge. bool_or over zero rows is
-- NULL, which is precisely the distinction between "attested as not a separator"
-- and "never attested", so the text test runs ONLY for ids the substrate cannot
-- answer for. Seeded, that is no ids and the fallback costs nothing; unseeded, it
-- is exactly the pre-existing behaviour.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION corpus_whitespace_vocab_indices(p_vocab bytea[])
    RETURNS TABLE(vocab_idx int)
    LANGUAGE sql STABLE PARALLEL SAFE
    AS $$
    SELECT (v.ord::int4 - 1) AS vocab_idx
    FROM unnest(p_vocab) WITH ORDINALITY v(id, ord)
    LEFT JOIN LATERAL (
        SELECT bool_or(cn.name IN ('unicode/category/Zs/v1',
                                   'unicode/category/Zl/v1',
                                   'unicode/category/Zp/v1',
                                   'unicode/category/Cc/v1')) AS is_sep
        FROM @extschema@.attestations a
        JOIN @extschema@.canonical_names cn ON cn.id = a.object_id
        WHERE a.subject_id = v.id
          AND a.type_id = @extschema@.relation_type_id('HAS_GENERAL_CATEGORY')
    ) g ON true
    WHERE COALESCE(g.is_sep, @extschema@.is_all_whitespace(@extschema@.render_text_fast(v.id, 8)))
$$;
